Bug 2083354 - Fix crash in [@ nsWindowWatcher::OpenWindowInternal]. r=tobyp

Always open a new content tab when Gecko requests a new window.

nsBrowserAccess._openURIInNewTab is called without a URI when Gecko asks for
a new content window, so it opened a contentTab for about:blank. The
contentTab shouldSwitchTo then reused any existing content tab still showing
about:blank, and handed that tab's browsing context back to nsWindowWatcher
as if it were new. That trips the assertions in
nsWindowWatcher::OpenWindowInternal, e.g. the
SetOnePermittedSandboxedNavigator call failing when the reused tab had itself
been opened from a sandboxed document.

Pass duplicate whenever an nsIOpenWindowInfo is given, so a fresh tab is
always created for it.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334862

diff --git a/mail/base/content/browserRequest.js b/mail/base/content/browserRequest.js
--- a/mail/base/content/browserRequest.js
+++ b/mail/base/content/browserRequest.js
@@ -169,8 +169,9 @@ window.browserDOMWindow = new (class nsB
     const tabmail = win.document.getElementById("tabmail");
     const newTab = tabmail.openTab("contentTab", {
       background: loadInBackground,
       csp: aCsp,
+      duplicate: !!aOpenWindowInfo,
       linkHandler: aMessageManagerGroup,
       openWindowInfo: aOpenWindowInfo,
       referrerInfo: aReferrerInfo,
       skipLoad: aSkipLoad,
diff --git a/mail/base/content/mailWindow.js b/mail/base/content/mailWindow.js
--- a/mail/base/content/mailWindow.js
+++ b/mail/base/content/mailWindow.js
@@ -826,8 +826,9 @@ nsBrowserAccess.prototype = {
     const tabmail = win.document.getElementById("tabmail");
     const newTab = tabmail.openTab("contentTab", {
       background: loadInBackground,
       csp: aCsp,
+      duplicate: !!aOpenWindowInfo,
       linkHandler: aMessageManagerGroup,
       openWindowInfo: aOpenWindowInfo,
       referrerInfo: aReferrerInfo,
       skipLoad: aSkipLoad,
